{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgVF5CcC1Sej5ra4BrhTi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, it did. The claims named a column and a date rule, and the defaults chose a 29 Feb policy. The causes were findings from running the code. They belong to the diagnosis, not to the problem. Here is the problem without them.\n\n## Hypothesis\nA customer's reminder arrives 14 days before their renewal. For some customers it doesn't.\n\nThis would be false if every customer's reminder were exactly 14 days before their renewal. Two customers show it isn't.\n\n## What was observed\n- **C-327:** the reminder was sent on 2024-05-17. The customer says their renewal is June 1, so the gap was 15 days.\n- **C-311:** the reminder was sent on 2026-10-19. The customer says they moved to annual in March, so the reminder is earlier than they expected.\n- **C-340 and C-302:** the dates look right to me. I didn't check them against the customers themselves.\n\n## What is not settled\n- **What counts as the renewal date.** For C-327 the customer states it. For C-311 nobody has said what their renewal date is, so I don't know whether 2026-10-19 is wrong by days or by months.\n- **Where the wrong dates come from.** I found candidate causes in the code (the start-date column, the 365-day year, and only the first anniversary being computed). I now treat them as leads for the fix, not as part of the problem.\n\n## Claims (outcomes only)\n- **Gap of 14 days.**\n  - Example: C-327 renews June 1, 2024, so the reminder is on May 18.\n  - Falsified if: any customer has a gap other than 14 days.\n- **Reminder only for a renewal that belongs to the customer.**\n  - Example: C-311 gets no reminder on 2026-10-19.\n  - Falsified if: C-311 is still reminded then.\n  - It needs one answer from you, below.\n- **No change for the others.**\n  - Example: C-340 stays at 2026-01-06 and C-302 at 2025-08-01.\n  - Falsified if: either date changes.\n\n## Decide\n**What is C-311's actual renewal date?**\n- **Option A:** one year after they moved to annual, which is 2027-03-10. I expect this, because it matches their complaint, but it is a guess.\n- **Option B:** something else, such as a billing date I can't see here.\n\nThis is the only question that evidence raised. The rest stay open until the fix is designed: which date counts as the plan start, how 29 Feb is handled, and what happens to multi-year customers.\n\n## Not explored\nThe nightly sender, the live table, and time zones. I have not confirmed that multi-year customers are affected.\n\nVote GO, NO-GO, or HOLD."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1815,"cache_read_input_tokens":41507,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1815},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"269b63cc-c8f2-4fee-bf57-81b7420e5ccd","uuid":"7989cec9-a790-4758-96a0-eb68432cbada","timestamp":"2026-10-28T20:11:19.954Z","request_id":"req_011CgVF5CNobxxmS2t7nVFkN"}
